ant to get out of this  I think the first time I thought I've  made a terrible mistake was the weekend  after I first got elected back in 2008 I  mean anyone who's doing any challenging  job will also go through Reflections on  oh you know what's you know how much  more can I do but I I realize how much  there is to do and  what we've been able to accomplish with  an extraordinary team of diverse  Canadians serving this country going  through some really tough times I mean  we started with Trump then we had a  pandemic and then we had convoys and war  in Ukraine  um you know there are there are really  big issues around the world right now  and Canadians  you know as I travel around the world  and talk with other world leaders  um they sort of Look At Me With Envy  because I get to serve Canadians and  Canadians are incredibly thoughtful and  positive and ambitious and we're well  positioned yes even though we're facing  really tough times right now like  everyone around the world  we're positioned we just we just hit  second in the world on battery supply  chains we're positioned to be a supplier  of energy in a net zero world that that  decades from now is going to be  essential we're moving towards green  steel green aluminum at a time when the  world needs it we've got a diverse open  population open to immigration and  growing population uh more than our G7  counterparts the world looks at Canada  and goes oh my God you guys are well  positioned and of course for us here at  home we don't pay much attention to that  we focus on the challenges we're facing  but there is so much to be proud of in  this country there's so much to know  that we are capable of meeting and  conquering any challenge that comes our  way that for me it is the greatest  privilege of my life to be able to serve  Canadians in this role and to know that  I'm going to get to do it for many more  years  all right prime minister thank you thank  you daughter
 

